       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. A single 1000 mg dose of sertraline is well above any dose with an established safety record, and you haven't given a clinical rationale. Since an error here could seriously harm the patient, I'd rather not place it without more information.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If 1000 mg was a typo:** Tell me the intended dose, such as 100 mg or 200 mg once daily, and I'll enter it now.\n- **If this is intentional:** Talk to pharmacy or the attending first. Then place the order directly through the standard process, which includes a pharmacist's review of high-dose overrides. If you give me the rationale and who approved it, I can reconsider.\n- **If the question is about a patient who has taken an overdose:** That needs toxicology or poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) and monitoring, not a scheduled daily order.\n\nI can also enter a dose within the recommended range right away if you'd like."
